WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:08.264
A business orders connectivity. Instead of disconnected handoffs, one guarded Orchestration AI Agent coordinates five specialist agents.

00:00:08.444 --> 00:00:13.095
The goal: less rework, faster activation, and a customer who knows what happens next.

00:00:13.995 --> 00:00:19.786
Intake saves the order and its event together. A stable request key prevents duplicate acceptance.

00:00:19.966 --> 00:00:25.788
Invalid requests return for correction. Accepted work stays traceable, without another manual handoff.

00:00:26.688 --> 00:00:34.165
The Validation AI Agent checks the site and capacity before planning. Catching bad references early prevents downstream rework.

00:00:34.345 --> 00:00:40.562
A wrong site needs customer confirmation. Missing capacity needs manager review, not an invented approval.

00:00:41.462 --> 00:00:48.157
The Decomposition AI Agent turns an approved product into linked service and resource orders. No repeated rekeying.

00:00:48.337 --> 00:00:54.583
Unsupported products stop at intake. Catalogue governance keeps new mappings under the accountable planner's control.

00:00:55.483 --> 00:01:01.520
The Provisioning AI Agent rechecks capacity, risk and the change window, then allocates resources once.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:08.563
A partner timeout activates the Fallout Recovery AI Agent. A policy conflict takes a different path: human review.

00:01:09.463 --> 00:01:17.289
The Fallout Recovery AI Agent handles one allowlisted timeout, retries once, and hands control back to the Provisioning AI Agent.

00:01:17.469 --> 00:01:23.592
For faults outside that playbook, the delivery design requires service-desk integration and an accountable human owner.

00:01:24.492 --> 00:01:29.392
The service manager approves or rejects high-risk work. Every decision is audited.

00:01:29.572 --> 00:01:35.173
Approval cannot create capacity. Partners cannot approve. Permitted work resumes its saved stage.

00:01:36.073 --> 00:01:43.743
After activation, the Customer Updates AI Agent persists Turkish and English portal confirmations. Clear status reduces chasing.

00:01:43.923 --> 00:01:51.257
The portal provides the customer record. Email and text delivery require integrated channel services and service-desk ownership.

00:01:52.157 --> 00:02:00.032
TM Forum inspired product and service contracts preserve linked handoffs. Authenticated partner tools enter the same guarded flow.

00:02:00.212 --> 00:02:08.275
Customer integration defines the exact schemas and conformance acceptance. Partner access never bypasses policy or human authority.

00:02:09.175 --> 00:02:15.355
The residency architecture places the customer workload on Azure Local at an approved Turkish operator site.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:23.458
Delivery requires supported local infrastructure, local inference, keys, logs and backups, with controlled egress and regulatory approval.

00:02:24.358 --> 00:02:30.990
External Azure services supply approved images, management and monitoring. Every metadata flow needs approval.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:39.537
Where platform metadata must also stay local, evaluate eligible disconnected operations, with its local control plane and support requirements.

00:02:40.437 --> 00:02:48.894
Early checks address avoidable rework. Linked identifiers remove rekeying. Durable handoffs and bounded recovery reduce unnecessary waiting.

00:02:49.074 --> 00:02:56.588
The customer objective is simple: shorter delivery, fewer avoidable exceptions, and a clear, accountable path from order to activation.
